{:edb/db-before-t 1477 :edb/db-after-t 1478 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534790 50 #inst "2026-10-08T06:59:15.382Z" 13194139534790 true] [17592186096367 1100 "Consider the diagram shown below, where $\\overrightarrow{PQ}=\\mathbf{a}$, $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{c}$. Find $\\overrightarrow{TS}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\mathbf{c}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1102/Source/Images/ee9aee4946e062b8a7ad1fae2e350d37.png)" 13194139534790 false] [17592186096367 1100 "Consider the diagram shown below, where $\\overrightarrow{PQ}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{c}.$ Find $\\overrightarrow{TS}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\mathbf{c}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/04ce04bf7c7f88d6578c74db0d7398a6d299d11bd9f60f4fc4b6e1bfb0129f3b.png)" 13194139534790 true] [17592186096367 1145 "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $S$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b$, or $\\mathbf c$.\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TP}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{PQ}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{QS}}}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1102/Source/Images/70335ddb9f1d79ca14b9138a4291465d.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TP}} = -\\mathbf{b}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{PQ}} = \\mathbf{a}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{QS}} = \\mathbf{c}\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1102/Source/Images/f5c06f75325a6ca44c7da008f6706fb2.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nTS^(→) &= TP^(→) + PQ^(→) + QS^(→) \\\\\n&=-b + a + c \\\\\n&= a - b + c\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534790 false] [17592186096367 1145 "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $S$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b,$ or $\\mathbf c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TP}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{PQ}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{QS}}}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/53940607b5cbf0220008e6e31ec60f2fd7fd2e4f70c5a8e95e7fcfd64064b095.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TP}} = -\\mathbf{b}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{PQ}} = \\mathbf{a}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{QS}} = \\mathbf{c}.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/810cce10eb330b1767a101d9107a9534c437daa123f13056a486a9fc96dbab89.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TS} & =\\overset{\\to }{TP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QS} \\\\  & =-b+a+c \\\\  & =a-b+c.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534790 true] [17592186096409 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/2420154d44b786c6aad54212760e9a37ce67dbdce94a7043039f0e824c5ef9bc.png)\n\nIn parallelogram $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{CB}+\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{CA}$\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{CB}-\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\overrightarrow{AC}$\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{DC}=\\overrightarrow{BA}$" 13194139534790 true] [17592186096409 1100 "In parallelogram $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1102/Source/Images/38d6af513afb9edf4208166303e35ed3.png)\n\n1. $\\overrightarrow{CB}+\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{CA}$\n2. $\\overrightarrow{CB}-\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\overrightarrow{AC}$\n3. $\\overrightarrow{DC}=\\overrightarrow{BA}$" 13194139534790 false] [17592186096409 1145 "- Equality I is true. Indeed, $\\overrightarrow{CB}+\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{CA}$.\n- Equality II is false. Indeed,\n$CB^(→) - AB^(→)|= CB^(→) + BA^(→); = CA^(→); \\ne AC^(→)$\nsince $\\overrightarrow{CA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ have opposite directions.\n- Equality III is false. Indeed, $\\overrightarrow{DC}\\neq\\overrightarrow{BA}$ since they have opposite directions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534790 false] [17592186096409 1145 "- Equality I is true. Indeed, $\\overrightarrow{CB}+\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{CA}.$\n\n- Equality II is false. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CB}-\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BA} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CA} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{AC}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nsince $\\overrightarrow{CA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ have opposite directions.\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed, $\\overrightarrow{DC}\\neq\\overrightarrow{BA}$ since they have opposite directions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534790 true] [17592186096524 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/7431bd3281e4e49f4caaa5b701885fb64c58196b2256af9d8744decd9a0d0793.png)\n\n  \n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overrightarrow{PS}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{b},$ $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{c},$ and $\\overrightarrow{TS}=\\mathbf{d}.$ Find $\\overrightarrow{TQ}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b}, \\mathbf{c},$ and $\\mathbf{d}.$" 13194139534790 true] [17592186096524 1100 "Consider the diagram above, where $\\overrightarrow{PS}=\\mathbf{a}$, $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{b}$, $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{c}$, and $\\overrightarrow{TS}=\\mathbf{d}$. Find $\\overrightarrow{TQ}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b}, \\mathbf{c}$, and $\\mathbf{d}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1102/Source/Images/e1428d48e9b657cb65b4abaf82ef8e51.png)" 13194139534790 false] [17592186096524 1145 "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $Q$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b, \\mathbf c$, and $\\mathbf d$.\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TQ}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1102/Source/Images/d79b0f30be6e0809efe831e4862b1043.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TS}} = \\mathbf{d}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}} = -\\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1102/Source/Images/20b51829636015f084208e464d30bea9.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nTQ^(→) &= TS^(→) + SQ^(→) \\\\\n&= d + (-b) \\\\\n&= d - b\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534790 false] [17592186096524 1145 "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $Q$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b, \\mathbf c,$ and $\\mathbf d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition, \n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TQ}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/4902397acd28e2e5f85063ba55c576d3768360225a705f31a66bd460405dd5a6.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TS}} = \\mathbf{d}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}} = -\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/08086f7e09568f908aa4919a1156d52e465216221be8908e72a1fd90ec8843dd.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{TS}+\\overset{\\to }{SQ} \\\\  & =d+(-b) \\\\  & =d-b.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534790 true] [17592186096568 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310315 13194139534790 true] [17592186096568 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310322 13194139534790 true] [17592186096568 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310329 13194139534790 true] [17592186096568 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310354 13194139534790 true] [17592186096568 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310367 13194139534790 true] [17592186096612 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310336 13194139534790 true] [17592186096612 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310343 13194139534790 true] [17592186096612 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310377 13194139534790 true] [17592186096612 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310384 13194139534790 true] [17592186096713 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310350 13194139534790 true] [17592186096713 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310357 13194139534790 true] [17592186096713 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310360 13194139534790 true] [17592186096713 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310363 13194139534790 true] [17592186096713 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310370 13194139534790 true] [17592186097260 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534790 true] [17592186097260 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/f25561a25abf75f301cbd29c6d6c0e2a0b61a389b757c06cd883819642f30545.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCEF$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $\\overset{\\to }{BF}?$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{FA}-\\overset{\\to }{BA}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CF}$" 13194139534790 true] [17592186097260 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1102/Source/Images/q-69538.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCEF$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $BF^(→)$?\n\n1. $BC^(→) + CE^(→) + EF^(→)$\n2. $FA^(→) - BA^(→)$\n3. $BC^(→) + CF^(→)$" 13194139534790 false] [17592186097260 1145 "- For the $1$st expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF} & =(\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CE})+\\overset{\\to }{EF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BF}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $2$nd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{FA}-\\overset{\\to }{BA} & =\\overset{\\to }{FA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{FB} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{BF}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $3$rd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CF} & =\\overset{\\to }{BF}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." 13194139534790 true] [17592186310315 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310316 13194139534790 true] [17592186310315 1089 "q-141480" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310315 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534790 true] [17592186310315 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/0c681289ee631de241f876091878b84cd9497c5d8e71d27512f9a832c242329b.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{RS}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RP}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{QS}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310315 1113 #uuid "aba9a00f-cb4d-5b06-bebd-53c73877d87c" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310315 1145 "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $S$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ \n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QS}=\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PR}+\\overset{\\to }{RS}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/317d78cec35bc3721ebbd64ac1ed53aa5b36c89101a170b93805d17c670f2673.png)\n\n  \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PR}=-d,\\,\\overset{\\to }{RT}=b.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/ff4b4292bb8a15551cb22da1f621684e9fdf24d35ae873b408dc612e5b3255e8.png)\n\n   \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QS} & =\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PR}+\\overset{\\to }{RS} \\\\  & =a-d+b.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310316 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310317 13194139534790 true] [17592186310316 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310318 13194139534790 true] [17592186310316 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310319 13194139534790 true] [17592186310316 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310320 13194139534790 true] [17592186310316 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310321 13194139534790 true] [17592186310316 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534790 true] [17592186310316 1041 "selection" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310316 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310318 13194139534790 true] [17592186310316 1110 #uuid "c546faf8-d832-5368-8cde-e5abf5bac0e4" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310317 1034 "\\overset{\\to }{QS}=a-b+c" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310317 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534790 true] [17592186310317 1111 #uuid "2b8f1354-12e1-5e43-9647-e79310cb3bb3" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310318 1034 "\\overset{\\to }{QS}=a-d+b" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310318 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534790 true] [17592186310318 1111 #uuid "948f1841-a0bd-56e6-83e4-8832901c1955" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310319 1034 "\\overset{\\to }{QS}=a+b+c" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310319 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534790 true] [17592186310319 1111 #uuid "8406969e-b665-5965-a09c-709e8b3b8aa5" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310320 1034 "\\overset{\\to }{QS}=c-d+b" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310320 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534790 true] [17592186310320 1111 #uuid "bca5ee0c-3394-5047-bea7-02ec4533048b" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310321 1034 "\\overset{\\to }{QS}=b+d+c" 1319413