.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/90749b45c5e992ba17f09c6a3597adebcdad2ab9d354b2aee7e41058af69863a.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RP} & =\\overset{\\to }{RQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QP} \\\\  & =d+a.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310358 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310359 13194139534790 true] [17592186310358 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534790 true] [17592186310358 1041 "field-1" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310358 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310359 13194139534790 true] [17592186310358 1110 #uuid "ade2e86c-86a0-5c20-8f8d-2be6dd14299e" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310359 1034 "d+a" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310359 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534790 true] [17592186310359 1111 #uuid "95a3eb68-2bfa-5f72-862a-64a4c903b7fc" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310360 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310361 13194139534790 true] [17592186310360 1089 "q-328066" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310360 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534790 true] [17592186310360 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/0eccac1629f5ab7d80fe4a7a6d4b1f58867adeed023e957f1f52daa885a745fa.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{UP}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{UT}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{RQ}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{RQ}=$ \n {{field-1}}" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310360 1113 #uuid "ceacc4af-4ece-5930-b5ef-87e857f1b68c" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310360 1145 "We want to find a \"path\" from $R$ to $Q$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{RQ}=\\overset{\\to }{RP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/c3abc51a0c48faa7853eb2ef605412ca6311866994b15a579b7bc7e7db63ee15.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{RP}=-d,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=-a.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/a53de4a8dcbd4a5d1f7640d5e1d4c8b6fd6e5e24388f432d279392727b11dd59.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{RP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =-d+(-a) \\\\  & =-d-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310361 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310362 13194139534790 true] [17592186310361 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534790 true] [17592186310361 1041 "field-1" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310361 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310362 13194139534790 true] [17592186310361 1110 #uuid "f9cda418-315a-51b2-83f5-c2dddd2b4c42" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310362 1034 "-d-a" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310362 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534790 true] [17592186310362 1111 #uuid "4bc84880-6e9a-5753-b9ca-312573979730" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310363 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310364 13194139534790 true] [17592186310363 1089 "q-328086" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310363 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534790 true] [17592186310363 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/6709c80eeddea3d31d68d51816a0249758d5a535eb5f2e6983f8e786faf3f227.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{PS}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{TS}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{QT}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{QT}=$ \n {{field-1}}" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310363 1113 #uuid "c081346a-0e68-599c-87e2-af148437aebf" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310363 1145 "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $T$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QT}=\\overset{\\to }{QS}+\\overset{\\to }{ST},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/cd8dc0d2e01927c8b2ca116265b257d835a1baae62272b703610f2947d92a8c2.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QS}=-b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{ST}=-c.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/8ed8c71e0d45ae0c9cf7d8a7d2889ee3a79471aaeb408ad0f53f487523daac13.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QT} & =\\overset{\\to }{QS}+\\overset{\\to }{ST} \\\\  & =-b+(-c) \\\\  & =-b-c.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310364 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310365 13194139534790 true] [17592186310364 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310366 13194139534790 true] [17592186310364 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534790 true] [17592186310364 1041 "field-1" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310364 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310365 13194139534790 true] [17592186310364 1110 #uuid "e351ee66-0add-5f2c-8052-3aeed686e669" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310365 1034 "-b-c" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310365 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534790 true] [17592186310365 1111 #uuid "dea8b1e2-5c3b-5aaa-b2f0-a3528c417c58" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310366 1034 "b+c" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310366 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534790 true] [17592186310366 1111 #uuid "3db78896-d0f1-5cce-a610-5fc6317807b4" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310367 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310368 13194139534790 true] [17592186310367 1089 "q-335826" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310367 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534790 true] [17592186310367 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/4ad1c49955142936f8b6fef257af8021e4eb9aa576cd37ebed149e5a31fbedc8.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{EF}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{GE}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{AF}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{GC}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ in terms of  $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{AC}=$   \n {{field-1}}" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310367 1113 #uuid "649372db-d035-5c8c-959e-85806024367f" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310367 1145 "We want to find a \"path\" from $A$ to $C$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{AC}=\\overset{\\to }{AF}+\\overset{\\to }{FE}+\\overset{\\to }{EG}+\\overset{\\to }{GC}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/e24ac0b6cf4f039cd1e8b2e1aa5dd921ea637fb2fe46666a0091372dfce87d44.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{AF}=c,\\,\\overset{\\to }{FE}=-a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{EG}=-b\\,\\overset{\\to }{GC}=d.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/37c3758dc7a4c8a5b79c3e687e77f62090282410e3bf45bfade3494cd3b8055b.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AC} & =\\overset{\\to }{AF}+\\overset{\\to }{FE}+\\overset{\\to }{EG}+\\overset{\\to }{GC} \\\\  & =c+(-a)+(-b)+d \\\\  & =c-a-b+d.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310369 13194139534790 true] [17592186310368 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534790 true] [17592186310368 1041 "field-1" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310368 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310369 13194139534790 true] [17592186310368 1110 #uuid "be832db7-8c94-5e8f-9f67-0a036205dc86" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310369 1034 "c-a-b+d" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310369 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534790 true] [17592186310369 1111 #uuid "b72b5961-3ab4-5ad8-9ea7-fc582874d0bb" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310370 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310371 13194139534790 true] [17592186310370 1089 "q-69531" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310370 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534790 true] [17592186310370 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/0236def5e17743a95be036e4f3c7b0dcf1a5c150ef53e56464f06afd6afcb5ca.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{PS}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{QS}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{PT}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{QT}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{TS}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310370 1113 #uuid "63ca1857-38b6-52de-8357-584a5f9bcc84" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310370 1145 "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $S$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition, \n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{TS}=\\overset{\\to }{TP}+\\overset{\\to }{PS},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/6d9225f220f50031fcbc7680c697b31eb8ce7733f07b83713c0dbe0c2ad89490.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{TP}=-c,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PS}=a.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/533805fc0d558bde49590a6dd82414de22efeeadbc76e91760bea33bcd0ceeff.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TS} & =\\overset{\\to }{TP}+\\overset{\\to }{PS} \\\\  & =-c+a \\\\  & =a-c.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310371 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310372 13194139534790 true] [17592186310371 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310