gure $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $\\overset{\\to }{DB}?$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BA}-\\overset{\\to }{CA}+\\overset{\\to }{CD}$" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310377 1113 #uuid "9fba8117-2a8c-5edb-aca0-764fe3cd4be5" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310377 1145 "- For the $1$st expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB} & =(\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC})+\\overset{\\to }{CB} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $2$nd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $3$rd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BA}-\\overset{\\to }{CA}+\\overset{\\to }{CD} & =(\\overset{\\to }{BA}-\\overset{\\to }{CA})+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =(\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC})+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BD} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{DB}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." 13194139534790 true] [17592186310378 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310379 13194139534790 true] [17592186310378 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310380 13194139534790 true] [17592186310378 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310381 13194139534790 true] [17592186310378 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310382 13194139534790 true] [17592186310378 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310383 13194139534790 true] [17592186310378 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534790 true] [17592186310378 1041 "selection" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310378 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310382 13194139534790 true] [17592186310378 1110 #uuid "6e437920-4dba-5cd2-81e5-92329f33c30a" 13194139534790 true] [17592186310379 1034 "II and III only" 131941395347